</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Why is colonosocpy more difficult in women?</article-title><source>Gastrointest Endosc</source><year>1996</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>124</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8635705</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0016-5107(96)70317-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Gonzalez</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Messina</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Pollack</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Factors that predict colonoscopy: thinner is not always better</article-title><source>Am J Gastroenterol</source><year>2000</year><volume>95</volume><fpage>2784</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11051348</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1572-0241.2000.03186.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dafnis</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Granath</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Pahlman</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Ekbom</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Blomqvist</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patient factors influencing the completion rate in colonoscopies</article-title><source>Dig Liv Dis</source><year>2005</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>113</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.dld.2004.09.015</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chak</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>GS</given-names